<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamilakam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamilakam was the ancient Tamil country of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, covering roughly modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> and adjacent areas. In the Sangam age it was shared by the three crowned dynasties, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chera-dynasty">Cheras</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>, together with many lesser chiefs. It was united by language and a common literature, the poetry of the Sangam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamilakam.jpg" alt="Tamilakam" width="320" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yon Man33 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_India_in_Sangam_Period.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
